(iii) We did not design and maintain effective controls over the accounting for revenue from contracts with customers. Specifically, we did not formally document controls in place within the revenue cycle, including controls over our estimation process for the allowance for price concessions and controls to assess principal versus agent considerations within our revenue arrangements. This material weakness resulted in the restatement of our previously-issued financial statements and other audit adjustments that were immaterial;

